<%# Operator menu reply (Uplink::PunishmentsController, the pin and
    reaction refusals too): appended to the acting viewer's #toast-region
    in the turbo_stream response, so it never reaches another viewer.
    Locals: message, error (true = the action was refused), kicker
    (optional, MODERATION by default). The toast controller
    auto-dismisses it; it announces no channel, so the shell leaves it
    alone. %>
<div class="toast toast--moderation<%= " toast--moderation-error" if error %>" role="status"
  data-controller="toast" data-action="click->toast#dismiss">
  <div class="toast-kicker toast-kicker--moderation"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:kicker, "MODERATION") %></div>
  <div class="toast-title"><%= message %></div>
</div>
